## Development

<details>
<summary>Prerequisites</summary>

1. [Install uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/).
{%- if with_databricks %}
2. Install Java 17 (required for PySpark/Databricks Connect):
   - **macOS**: 
     ```sh
     brew install openjdk@17
     ```
     Add to your shell profile (e.g., `~/.zshrc`):
     ```sh
     export JAVA_HOME="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17"
     export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/bin:$PATH"
     ```
   - **Ubuntu**: `sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk`
   - **Windows**: Download from [Adoptium](https://adoptium.net/)
{%- endif %}

</details>

<details open>
<summary>Development environment setup</summary>

Clone this repository and run the following from root of the repository:

```sh
# Create and install a virtual environment
uv sync --all-extras

# Install the pre-commit hooks
pre-commit install --install-hooks
```

</details>

<details open>
<summary>Developing</summary>

- Run `poe` from within the development environment to print a list of [Poe the Poet](https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet) tasks available to run on this project.
- Run `uv add {package}` from within the development environment to install a run time dependency and add it to `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. Add `--dev` to install a development dependency.
- Run `uv sync --upgrade` from within the development environment to upgrade all dependencies to the latest versions allowed by `pyproject.toml`. Add `--only-dev` to upgrade the development dependencies only.

</details>
